  "plan": "## Implementation Plan: Add Code Path to Board\n\n### Overview\nThis feature adds explicit `code_path` configuration to each project and creates a `<project_root>/.mad/CONTEXT.md` file for project-level context. Agents will be invoked from the project root with knowledge of the code path and context file location.\n\n### Components\n\n#### 1. Config Schema Changes\n- Add `code_path` field to `<project_root>/.mad.config.json`\n- Add `context_file` field pointing to `<project_root>/.mad/CONTEXT.md` (computed, not stored)\n- Store `code_path` as-is; resolve symlinks at read time using `os.path.realpath()`\n- If `code_path` not set in per-board config, fall back to default location\n- No config version/migration needed\n\n#### 2. CONTEXT.md File\n- Location: `<project_root>/.mad/CONTEXT.md`\n- Optional: missing file is OK, just ignore\n- Max size: 100KB - truncate or error if exceeded (implementation detail: truncate with warning)\n- If file cannot be read (permission denied, missing), silently ignore\n\n#### 3. Agent Invocation Changes\n- When starting a new agent session:\n  1. Set agent's working directory to `code_path` (project root), not the board's item directory\n  2. Prepend to agent's initial instruction/prompt:\n     - `Code Path: <resolved_code_path>`\n     - `Context File: <project_root>/.mad/CONTEXT.md`\n- This applies only to new agent sessions, not every turn in a conversation\n\n#### 4. CLI Commands (Required, Not Optional)\n- `mad context edit` - Open CONTEXT.md in editor\n- `mad context view` - Display current CONTEXT.md content\n- `mad config set code_path <path>` - Set code_path in `<project_root>/.mad.config.json`\n- `mad config get code_path` - Display current code_path\n\n#### 5. Path Resolution Logic\n- Read `code_path` from `<project_root>/.mad.config.json`\n- If not set, check per-board config\n- Resolve symlinks at read time: `os.path.realpath(code_path)`\n- Allow non-existent paths (for new projects)\n- Validation: document that security considerations exist but defer for now (create tracking item)\n\n### Files to Modify\n- Config loading/saving logic to support `<project_root>/.mad.config.json`\n- Agent invocation code to set working directory and prepend instructions\n- CLI commands for context viewing/editing and code_path management\n\n### Testing\n- Unit tests for config read/write with code_path\n- Integration tests for agent invocation with correct working directory\n- CLI tests for context and config commands"
